1
00:02:31,949 --> 00:02:34,469
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece

2
00:02:34,469 --> 00:02:37,389
must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

3
00:02:37,389 --> 00:02:41,709
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

4
00:02:41,709 --> 00:02:44,789
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber

5
00:02:44,789 --> 00:02:46,389
after eating the gum gum fruit,

6
00:02:46,389 --> 00:02:50,229
sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

7
00:02:50,229 --> 00:02:53,909
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

8
00:02:57,029 --> 00:02:59,669
Two years have passed since the War of the Best

9
00:02:59,669 --> 00:03:00,909
and Marineford.

10
00:03:00,909 --> 00:03:03,269
Luffy and his crew underwit special training

11
00:03:03,269 --> 00:03:06,749
before reuniting to continue on to the New World.

12
00:03:06,749 --> 00:03:09,989
They are now separated once again on Fishman Island,

13
00:03:09,989 --> 00:03:11,789
thousands of feet below sea level.

14
00:03:18,789 --> 00:03:19,789
Let's go!

15
00:03:19,789 --> 00:03:20,549
Break through!

16
00:03:24,429 --> 00:03:26,069
We're off to the sea forest!

17
00:03:29,669 --> 00:03:33,269
The Ryugu Palace in shock!

18
00:03:33,269 --> 00:03:35,309
The kidnapping of Shirahoshi!

19
00:03:41,709 --> 00:03:43,309
Thank you for making the trip.

20
00:03:43,309 --> 00:03:45,149
I don't get many visitors from above.

21
00:03:45,149 --> 00:03:46,789
No problem!

22
00:03:46,789 --> 00:03:49,949
When Tom told me his kid brother back home was also a shipwright,

23
00:03:49,949 --> 00:03:51,389
I knew I had to visit.

24
00:03:51,389 --> 00:03:55,869
Still, traveling to Fishman Island's a pretty difficult task.

25
00:03:55,869 --> 00:03:57,909
Heh, it's not bad.

26
00:03:57,909 --> 00:04:00,069
Training with Tom since I was young paid off.

27
00:04:00,069 --> 00:04:03,269
My crewmates and I made it here on a ship that I built!

28
00:04:03,269 --> 00:04:04,669
Is that so?

29
00:04:04,669 --> 00:04:06,709
Well, you were my brother's pupil.

30
00:04:06,709 --> 00:04:08,509
It must be a fine vessel.

31
00:04:08,509 --> 00:04:09,109
Yeah!

32
00:04:09,109 --> 00:04:12,189
The Thousand Sunny will take us anywhere we want to go!

33
00:04:12,189 --> 00:04:14,949
It's my life's work, my masterpiece!

34
00:04:14,949 --> 00:04:17,189
I'd love to see it before you leave.

35
00:04:17,189 --> 00:04:19,189
Yeah, about that.

36
00:04:19,189 --> 00:04:20,829
After we got to Fishman Island,

37
00:04:20,829 --> 00:04:22,669
the Sunny was swept away by the tide.

38
00:04:22,669 --> 00:04:26,069
It's one of the reasons I came to see you.

39
00:04:26,069 --> 00:04:28,349
You know the area much better than I do.

40
00:04:28,349 --> 00:04:30,949
You have any idea where the ship might have turned up?

41
00:04:30,949 --> 00:04:33,349
Trust me, you'll find it.

42
00:04:33,349 --> 00:04:36,349
But where do I even start?

43
00:04:36,349 --> 00:04:38,989
It's a funny thing, but when ships sink around these parts,

44
00:04:38,989 --> 00:04:42,089
the tide almost always carries them to the same place.

45
00:04:42,089 --> 00:04:45,289
The Sunny is bound to be there too, I guarantee it.

46
00:04:45,289 --> 00:04:46,829
With gusto, even.

47
00:04:46,829 --> 00:04:48,789
You're that confident, huh?

48
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:51,369
Don't worry, we'll get there soon enough.

49
00:04:51,369 --> 00:04:53,409
On to the sea forest.

50
00:04:53,409 --> 00:04:55,209
The sea forest?

51
00:04:55,209 --> 00:05:00,249
Hold on, Luffy, what are you doing?

52
00:05:00,249 --> 00:05:00,909
Stop!

53
00:05:00,909 --> 00:05:03,089
Megalo, come back here now!

54
00:05:03,089 --> 00:05:05,589
Stay in the palace!

55
00:05:05,589 --> 00:05:10,489
Father, brothers, all my caretakers, forgive me.

56
00:05:10,489 --> 00:05:12,949
I'm leaving without your permission.

57
00:05:12,949 --> 00:05:21,829
I promise to be home by dinner.

58
00:05:21,829 --> 00:05:25,829
We're on an adventure!

59
00:05:25,829 --> 00:05:28,629
What has gotten into Megalo?

60
00:05:28,629 --> 00:05:31,729
I can't believe it, he even left the doors open.

61
00:05:31,729 --> 00:05:34,169
What if something were to happen to...

62
00:05:34,169 --> 00:05:35,169
Oh no!

63
00:05:35,169 --> 00:05:38,209
Hey, Skeleton, hurry up and check on the princess.

64
00:05:38,209 --> 00:05:41,149
All right, stop writing my bones about it.

65
00:05:47,089 --> 00:05:48,089
She's gone!

66
00:05:48,089 --> 00:05:50,889
Princess Shirohoshi never leaves her room!

67
00:05:50,889 --> 00:05:51,849
Oh no!

68
00:05:51,849 --> 00:05:54,429
But why are you keeping her locked up here in the first place?

69
00:05:54,429 --> 00:05:55,589
To keep her safe!

70
00:05:55,589 --> 00:05:57,429
Enemies are trying to get to her!

71
00:05:57,429 --> 00:05:58,329
Kidnap you!

72
00:05:58,329 --> 00:05:59,969
I'm sorry I failed you.

73
00:05:59,969 --> 00:06:02,209
Who knows how far away the kidnappers are!

74
00:06:02,209 --> 00:06:03,669
Kidnappers?

75
00:06:03,669 --> 00:06:07,109
Princess Shirohoshi!

76
00:06:07,109 --> 00:06:09,049
Forgive me!

77
00:06:09,049 --> 00:06:10,949
You're positive she was kidnapped?

78
00:06:10,949 --> 00:06:11,949
Huh?

79
00:06:11,949 --> 00:06:12,949
Huh!

80
00:06:12,949 --> 00:06:14,449
How rude of you!

81
00:06:14,449 --> 00:06:15,049
Ah!

82
00:06:19,049 --> 00:06:22,749
The gate connecting Fishman Island to the Ryugu Palace.

83
00:06:22,749 --> 00:06:25,129
Tell us where the switch to open it is or else.

84
00:06:25,129 --> 00:06:26,929
Wait, switch?

85
00:06:26,929 --> 00:06:27,789
Skeleton!

86
00:06:27,789 --> 00:06:30,829
You have to get back to King Nepune as fast as possible!

87
00:06:30,829 --> 00:06:33,769
Tell him the princess is gone, and that we're under attack!

88
00:06:33,769 --> 00:06:38,169
We didn't want any of this to happen, but it's the only way.

89
00:06:38,169 --> 00:06:41,509
They told us that if we want to survive, we've got to follow their orders.

90
00:06:44,069 --> 00:06:46,109
Please, just tell us, okay?

91
00:06:46,109 --> 00:06:47,349
Whose orders?

92
00:06:47,349 --> 00:06:48,589
It doesn't matter!

93
00:06:48,589 --> 00:06:50,709
Just tell us so we're all gonna die!

94
00:06:50,709 --> 00:06:51,349
I don't...

95
00:06:51,349 --> 00:06:53,949
Just tell us!

96
00:06:53,949 --> 00:06:55,949
What in the world is going on here?

97
00:07:00,829 --> 00:07:02,369
What in the world is going on here!

98
00:07:02,369 --> 00:07:03,669
Again, count.

99
00:07:03,669 --> 00:07:05,409
Unfortunately, we'll crack on the Juse Woody.

100
00:07:05,409 --> 00:07:06,629
How'd you make this?

101
00:07:06,869 --> 00:07:07,409
How can you see them?

102
00:07:07,409 --> 00:07:08,709
We'll give you...

103
00:07:08,709 --> 00:07:09,329
Ah!

104
00:07:09,329 --> 00:07:10,209
Professional Monkey is...

105
00:07:10,209 --> 00:07:10,709
I've lost sightseeing.

106
00:07:10,709 --> 00:07:11,709
These guys are...

107
00:07:11,709 --> 00:07:12,209
So useless!

108
00:07:12,209 --> 00:07:13,509
Humans really are pathetic, aren't they...

109
00:07:13,509 --> 00:07:16,069
Put them in the water and they just drown!

110
00:07:16,069 --> 00:07:23,849
You pirates are now under the control of Horty Jones, so listen closely.

111
00:07:24,249 --> 00:07:25,989
I've got wonderful news.

112
00:07:26,229 --> 00:07:29,029
You have the chance to be part of a historic mission.

113
00:07:29,489 --> 00:07:30,449
Talk about lucky.

114
00:07:31,209 --> 00:07:32,529
That looks like Van Der Decken.

115
00:07:33,049 --> 00:07:35,129
Isn't he the captain of the Flying Dutchman?

116
00:07:35,609 --> 00:07:36,709
This can't be real.

117
00:07:36,969 --> 00:07:38,609
That cursed ghost ship is a myth.

118
00:07:38,609 --> 00:07:40,949
Oh, I'm no ghost.

119
00:07:41,209 --> 00:07:43,609
But I am Van Der Decken's descendant.

120
00:07:43,609 --> 00:07:46,129
I've got a curse of my own as well.

121
00:07:46,369 --> 00:07:48,689
Even though I'm a fishman, I can't swim.

122
00:07:49,149 --> 00:07:50,349
But that's all right.

123
00:07:50,529 --> 00:07:53,789
I've got this devil fruit power known as the Mark Mark fruit.

124
00:07:54,169 --> 00:07:55,729
How about I show you?

125
00:07:57,929 --> 00:07:59,729
You and the stripes.

126
00:08:00,029 --> 00:08:00,549
Come here.

127
00:08:01,009 --> 00:08:01,909
Step right up.

128
00:08:02,129 --> 00:08:02,409
Me?

129
00:08:04,969 --> 00:08:05,569
Horty!

130
00:08:12,009 --> 00:08:12,649
Yeah.

131
00:08:12,649 --> 00:08:15,349
This is nonsense and you know it.

132
00:08:15,709 --> 00:08:16,709
Enough is enough.

133
00:08:19,749 --> 00:08:20,869
Is that Horty?

134
00:08:21,009 --> 00:08:22,109
What is he doing here?

135
00:08:23,489 --> 00:08:24,429
Hello there.

136
00:08:24,649 --> 00:08:28,169
Those energy steroids you're taking will do nothing but mess up your body.

137
00:08:28,709 --> 00:08:31,249
And no good can come of destroying Fishman Island.

138
00:08:31,749 --> 00:08:34,349
On top of it, you're underestimating the power of Neptune.

139
00:08:35,109 --> 00:08:35,549
Horty.

140
00:08:36,269 --> 00:08:38,229
I've heard enough of your rambling.

141
00:08:38,229 --> 00:08:41,369
I don't want to listen to your voice anymore.

142
00:08:41,369 --> 00:08:45,049
To think you were an officer of the pirate group that I admired.

143
00:08:45,829 --> 00:08:48,029
Now you're nothing but a washed up coward.

144
00:08:48,489 --> 00:08:51,009
So, make way for the real pirates.

145
00:08:51,009 --> 00:08:57,429
If we want to teach all of the humans a lesson, we're going to need Fishman Island.

146
00:08:57,709 --> 00:08:59,469
That means Neptune is our enemy.

147
00:09:00,469 --> 00:09:02,949
Arlong thought Fishman were the supreme race.

148
00:09:03,109 --> 00:09:04,649
When did you change your mind?

149
00:09:04,789 --> 00:09:05,769
Arlong was wrong.

150
00:09:05,869 --> 00:09:07,309
There is no supreme race.

151
00:09:07,849 --> 00:09:08,169
Deacon?

152
00:09:08,169 --> 00:09:11,089
Hyozo, why are you doing this?

153
00:09:11,529 --> 00:09:15,389
The two of you refused to help Arlong invade the East Blue when he was in power.

154
00:09:15,989 --> 00:09:19,429
So tell me, what makes you want to work with these young punks now?

155
00:09:20,509 --> 00:09:21,389
That's easy.

156
00:09:21,849 --> 00:09:22,789
I meant it for money.

157
00:09:23,109 --> 00:09:24,409
These guys are willing to pay.

158
00:09:26,189 --> 00:09:27,409
Arlong was stingy.

159
00:09:27,589 --> 00:09:30,469
He never did pony up enough dough to enlist my services.

160
00:09:31,109 --> 00:09:35,109
That's why he was always stuck taking crappy swordsmen like you, Along.

161
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:37,169
No wonder he lost.

162
00:09:37,169 --> 00:09:39,949
A sight for sore eyes.

163
00:09:40,129 --> 00:09:40,969
An angry Hachi.

164
00:09:41,549 --> 00:09:43,589
Yeah, I remember what happened back then.

165
00:09:43,989 --> 00:09:46,869
Arlong had the nerve to ask me to work underneath him.

166
00:09:47,529 --> 00:09:49,169
What a preposterous idea.

167
00:09:49,649 --> 00:09:51,769
Vander Decken never works under anybody.

168
00:09:51,969 --> 00:09:53,109
I'm my own man.

169
00:09:53,589 --> 00:09:55,409
Hordy gets that better than anyone.

170
00:09:57,009 --> 00:10:01,469
Arlong had goals and an ability to act on them, which I can respect.

171
00:10:07,169 --> 00:10:09,129
But he was also brash.

172
00:10:09,349 --> 00:10:11,549
As a leader, he was lacking in cunning.

173
00:10:11,549 --> 00:10:17,309
When you old-timers were running rampant on the sea, we were all still too young to become pirates.

174
00:10:17,669 --> 00:10:18,549
So we watched.

175
00:10:19,329 --> 00:10:22,069
We saw what you did well and what you did poorly.

176
00:10:22,509 --> 00:10:24,189
We learned from all your mistakes.

177
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:26,649
In that sense, we owe you our thanks.

178
00:10:26,649 --> 00:10:28,569
Take heart.

179
00:10:28,569 --> 00:10:31,229
I will continue right where Arlong left off.

180
00:10:31,229 --> 00:10:34,249
I don't understand why you're not on board with that.

181
00:10:34,649 --> 00:10:37,409
You supported Arlong for all those years, after all.

182
00:10:38,109 --> 00:10:40,289
What a disappointment you are, Hachi.

183
00:10:41,009 --> 00:10:42,429
You might want to know.

184
00:10:42,789 --> 00:10:47,249
The pirate who destroyed Arlong's dream, Straw Hat Luffy, is on Fishman Island.

185
00:10:47,249 --> 00:10:50,129
It's a perfect opportunity for some revenge.

186
00:10:50,769 --> 00:10:55,589
Even though I fought him as a member of the Arlong Pirates, he now calls me his friend.

187
00:10:56,129 --> 00:10:56,509
Look!

188
00:10:56,749 --> 00:10:58,669
All three of you are my friends now!

189
00:11:00,189 --> 00:11:02,569
Straw Hat Luffy also saved my life.

190
00:11:03,109 --> 00:11:05,209
If I could, I would see him.

191
00:11:07,909 --> 00:11:10,869
But I'm too ashamed of my fellow Fishman to do it!

192
00:11:11,109 --> 00:11:13,649
How can I face him when you're clinging to Arlong's legacy?

193
00:11:14,189 --> 00:11:16,229
You consider a human your friend?

194
00:11:16,229 --> 00:11:17,649
How pathetic!

195
00:11:18,289 --> 00:11:19,709
You're not a real fishman!

196
00:11:19,809 --> 00:11:20,949
Get out of my sight!

197
00:11:22,409 --> 00:11:24,649
Calm yourself and listen.

198
00:11:27,309 --> 00:11:30,569
You may have forgotten how pirates do things around here.

199
00:11:30,789 --> 00:11:35,649
If there's something you want to say, you've got to use violence to get your point across.

200
00:11:36,169 --> 00:11:36,789
For example!

201
00:11:37,869 --> 00:11:38,469
Watch!

202
00:11:39,409 --> 00:11:41,109
Where is he throwing it to?

203
00:11:41,549 --> 00:11:44,229
Did you notice when I touched you earlier,

204
00:11:44,229 --> 00:11:46,249
I marked you as my new target!

205
00:11:46,989 --> 00:11:49,749
No matter what I throw or where I throw it,

206
00:11:49,989 --> 00:11:52,989
it will always make its way back to whatever I mark.

207
00:11:53,209 --> 00:11:56,309
Not only that, but it'll come back at you full speed!

208
00:11:56,509 --> 00:11:57,529
I suspect!

209
00:11:57,529 --> 00:12:00,169
But that's crazy!

210
00:12:00,289 --> 00:12:02,429
Deacon just tossed the knife away from that guy!

211
00:12:02,529 --> 00:12:03,789
And it came back to hit him!

212
00:12:05,169 --> 00:12:07,049
The mark mark curse!

213
00:12:07,509 --> 00:12:10,049
Of course, there are some limitations.

214
00:12:10,529 --> 00:12:11,989
Can you figure them out?

215
00:12:12,529 --> 00:12:13,929
You had better hurry.

216
00:12:14,929 --> 00:12:16,509
Stay away from me, Deacon!

217
00:12:16,509 --> 00:12:19,949
I've heard enough stories about your mark mark power!

218
00:12:20,389 --> 00:12:21,649
You've got to make him stop!

219
00:12:21,769 --> 00:12:23,069
He's trying to kill me!

220
00:12:23,469 --> 00:12:24,929
Please stop him, Hordy!

221
00:12:26,009 --> 00:12:26,969
Sorry, Hachi.

222
00:12:27,169 --> 00:12:27,849
I can't.

223
00:12:28,249 --> 00:12:29,369
As he told you earlier,

224
00:12:29,709 --> 00:12:31,449
Vander Deacon isn't working under me.

225
00:12:31,889 --> 00:12:33,429
We're allies on equal footing.

226
00:12:34,109 --> 00:12:34,729
Besides,

227
00:12:35,449 --> 00:12:37,869
you're really starting to get on my nerves.

228
00:12:39,149 --> 00:12:40,609
Go ahead, Deacon!

229
00:12:40,609 --> 00:13:06,829
I'll be okay if I can just find my way to the exit!

230
00:13:10,609 --> 00:13:13,429
There, I should be safe now.

231
00:13:13,869 --> 00:13:15,289
Hopefully, they sink in the water.

232
00:13:19,069 --> 00:13:21,249
They burst through the bubble like it was nothing!

233
00:13:21,669 --> 00:13:22,369
Get away!

234
00:13:22,369 --> 00:13:22,869
Get away!

235
00:13:23,629 --> 00:13:23,669
Oh!

236
00:13:24,629 --> 00:13:26,029
Ah!

237
00:13:40,829 --> 00:13:41,829
Ah!

238
00:13:43,869 --> 00:13:45,809
Ah!

239
00:13:48,209 --> 00:13:49,989
Ah!

240
00:13:50,169 --> 00:13:50,489
Ah!

241
00:13:50,489 --> 00:13:50,829
Ah!

242
00:13:50,829 --> 00:13:51,009
Ah!

243
00:13:51,009 --> 00:13:52,249
Ah!

244
00:13:52,249 --> 00:14:22,229
To be continued...

245
00:14:22,249 --> 00:14:29,009
But yet, I can throw weapons and even my love, they'll track you down to the furthest depths of hell.

246
00:14:29,329 --> 00:14:31,529
That's the Mark Mark curse for you.

247
00:14:31,689 --> 00:14:35,549
Whoa. He can keep stalking the princess for as long as he wants.

248
00:14:35,849 --> 00:14:40,709
And stay right here. Best of all, he'll never have to deal with fighting Neptune and his sons.

249
00:14:40,969 --> 00:14:41,569
Bingo!

250
00:14:42,289 --> 00:14:44,189
How devious can you get?

251
00:14:46,249 --> 00:14:48,729
Now, about you human pirates.

252
00:14:48,729 --> 00:14:52,449
I'm sure you're all familiar with Deccan's Mark Mark power.

253
00:14:53,169 --> 00:14:56,109
So, let's begin the first stage of your mission.

254
00:14:59,509 --> 00:15:04,049
They say the Ryugu Palace is impregnable, but I disagree.

255
00:15:04,989 --> 00:15:11,029
Someone in this room has been able to break through its defenses for ten straight years.

256
00:15:11,549 --> 00:15:13,689
Him, Captain Vander Deccan.

257
00:15:13,689 --> 00:15:16,469
Bah! Ho, ho, ho, ho, ho, ho, ho, ho, ho!

258
00:15:17,129 --> 00:15:19,729
So, you'll be our cannon fodder.

259
00:15:20,069 --> 00:15:23,369
Meaning, Deccan will treat your bodies as living ammunition.

260
00:15:25,369 --> 00:15:28,209
Throwing you straight into the wall of the princess's tower.

261
00:15:29,209 --> 00:15:31,729
Of course, weapons can't smash it.

262
00:15:31,969 --> 00:15:33,789
And most of you runts won't do any better.

263
00:15:33,789 --> 00:15:40,289
And then, you'll open up the gate from inside the palace.

264
00:15:40,969 --> 00:15:43,009
Find the gate switch and let us in.

265
00:15:43,509 --> 00:15:44,889
That's all you have to do.

266
00:15:45,809 --> 00:15:47,909
No way! We can't make it that far!

267
00:15:48,249 --> 00:15:49,029
You're crazy!

268
00:15:49,429 --> 00:15:51,329
We'd already be dead from hitting the wall!

269
00:15:51,829 --> 00:15:52,829
You're correct.

270
00:15:53,169 --> 00:15:55,329
That's why I want you humans to do it.

271
00:15:55,749 --> 00:15:57,629
Your lives don't mean anything to me.

272
00:15:57,629 --> 00:16:01,369
In our world, you're either slaves or corpses.

273
00:16:02,349 --> 00:16:05,869
Those of you who survived the impact, carry out your duty.

274
00:16:06,109 --> 00:16:08,889
If you succeed in opening the gate, I'll set you free.

275
00:16:09,269 --> 00:16:11,949
But if you refuse to do it, then leave!

276
00:16:12,229 --> 00:16:13,889
I'll get you out of the bubble myself.

277
00:16:14,529 --> 00:16:16,289
So you better do as I say.

278
00:16:16,409 --> 00:16:20,969
But if... if we leave the bubble, we can't get to the top without drowning!

279
00:16:21,149 --> 00:16:22,089
Well, that's no good.

280
00:16:22,309 --> 00:16:25,709
On the upside, that should make this decision easy for you, though!

281
00:16:25,709 --> 00:16:26,109
Huh?

282
00:16:26,409 --> 00:16:26,689
Huh?

283
00:16:26,689 --> 00:16:28,469
Have fun!

284
00:16:35,429 --> 00:16:36,909
It's a new era.

285
00:16:37,289 --> 00:16:41,149
From now on, our people will forge a new history with our own hands.

286
00:16:42,769 --> 00:16:46,109
We'll start by conquering the Ryugu kingdom!

287
00:16:46,109 --> 00:16:46,969
Yeah!

288
00:16:49,929 --> 00:16:52,649
Shira Hoshi, just you wait!

289
00:16:52,649 --> 00:17:00,869
Meanwhile, back at the palace...

290
00:17:00,869 --> 00:17:04,029
Don't go so fast!

291
00:17:04,129 --> 00:17:04,869
We're injured!

292
00:17:05,289 --> 00:17:06,529
Pick up the pace, skeleton!

293
00:17:06,789 --> 00:17:08,569
It's imperative we make it to the king!

294
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:11,849
Listen, I'm begging you to take us to that gate!

295
00:17:12,069 --> 00:17:14,289
Party's gonna kill us all if we don't get it open!

296
00:17:14,429 --> 00:17:15,249
You have to!

297
00:17:17,909 --> 00:17:20,689
Hey, I have a question for you guys.

298
00:17:20,689 --> 00:17:23,089
Sanji, go back to bed!

299
00:17:23,089 --> 00:17:23,989
No fighting!

300
00:17:23,989 --> 00:17:25,349
I'm not fighting.

301
00:17:25,529 --> 00:17:28,169
I just want to ask them something about the Ryugu palace.

302
00:17:28,909 --> 00:17:29,969
Is she there?

303
00:17:30,509 --> 00:17:31,489
The mermaid princess?

304
00:17:31,869 --> 00:17:32,249
Yeah.

305
00:17:32,649 --> 00:17:33,429
She's there.

306
00:17:33,669 --> 00:17:34,329
So what?

307
00:17:34,329 --> 00:17:35,069
I'll go.

308
00:17:35,369 --> 00:17:36,049
It's worth it.

309
00:17:36,249 --> 00:17:37,029
No, it isn't!

310
00:17:37,289 --> 00:17:38,369
You're still too weak!

311
00:17:38,669 --> 00:17:40,469
If she's beautiful, you might die!

312
00:17:40,669 --> 00:17:41,449
Come on.

313
00:17:41,589 --> 00:17:43,169
Of course she's beautiful, right?

314
00:17:43,269 --> 00:17:44,669
Well, I've never seen her.

315
00:17:45,089 --> 00:17:46,929
But they do say she's quite lovely.

316
00:17:47,149 --> 00:17:47,829
She is?

317
00:17:48,109 --> 00:17:48,509
Right!

318
00:17:48,649 --> 00:17:49,749
Then lead the way!

319
00:17:50,409 --> 00:17:51,509
Let's stop fighting!

320
00:17:51,649 --> 00:17:52,129
Take me!

321
00:17:52,349 --> 00:17:53,929
Wait, which way is the palace?

322
00:17:54,189 --> 00:17:55,789
My true love awaits!

323
00:17:56,649 --> 00:17:57,929
What's wrong with this guy?

324
00:17:58,289 --> 00:18:00,789
I don't know, but we're supposed to take him in regardless.

325
00:18:01,209 --> 00:18:04,409
Before we depart for the palace, we need to handcuff you.

326
00:18:04,689 --> 00:18:06,429
If I can see her, who cares?

327
00:18:06,789 --> 00:18:08,569
Tie me up and take me away!

328
00:18:09,569 --> 00:18:10,749
You nutcase!

329
00:18:11,009 --> 00:18:11,889
Snap out of it!

330
00:18:11,929 --> 00:18:12,869
Don't go with them!

331
00:18:12,929 --> 00:18:13,409
Wait a minute!

332
00:18:14,149 --> 00:18:16,669
How am I supposed to cook for the mermaid princess

333
00:18:16,669 --> 00:18:18,829
if you put me in handcuffs, you imbeciles?

334
00:18:18,989 --> 00:18:20,369
That's why it's not okay!

335
00:18:20,949 --> 00:18:22,289
I knew he would resist!

336
00:18:22,709 --> 00:18:24,169
Everyone subdue the human!

337
00:18:24,669 --> 00:18:25,189
Bastards.

338
00:18:25,189 --> 00:18:27,869
Sabotaging my one chance to see the princess?

339
00:18:28,149 --> 00:18:29,689
I bet you're just jealous!

340
00:18:31,229 --> 00:18:32,109
Too bad!

341
00:18:32,709 --> 00:18:34,049
It can't help me!

342
00:18:36,649 --> 00:18:37,909
Hey, Sanji!

343
00:18:38,349 --> 00:18:39,249
Don't fight them!

344
00:18:39,289 --> 00:18:40,089
We gotta run!

345
00:18:40,429 --> 00:18:41,409
Or whatever.

346
00:18:41,949 --> 00:18:42,729
Beat them all up.

347
00:18:43,069 --> 00:18:43,329
Sure.

348
00:18:44,809 --> 00:18:47,429
Did you realize we were innocent before you did that?

349
00:18:48,469 --> 00:18:51,549
Well, it's their fault for trying to handcuff me.

350
00:18:52,189 --> 00:18:53,949
Their members are the Strollhats.

351
00:18:53,949 --> 00:18:55,529
How dangerous.

352
00:18:56,269 --> 00:18:57,269
Look at what you've done!

353
00:18:57,489 --> 00:18:59,789
Now everybody's giving us that dead fish stare!

354
00:18:59,989 --> 00:19:01,369
And not because they're fishmen either!

355
00:19:01,989 --> 00:19:03,229
That's not our problem.

356
00:19:03,569 --> 00:19:05,689
Besides, they saw the guards attack us.

357
00:19:05,689 --> 00:19:07,549
But you were the one doing all the attacking!

358
00:19:08,209 --> 00:19:10,309
Hey now, you beat up a lot of them too.

359
00:19:10,569 --> 00:19:12,089
Speaking of, good job.

360
00:19:12,309 --> 00:19:13,829
Your training really paid off.

361
00:19:13,989 --> 00:19:16,749
Oh, you think you can buy me off with a compliment?

362
00:19:17,089 --> 00:19:18,309
No way, pal.

363
00:19:18,309 --> 00:19:21,529
A lady is in need!

364
00:19:22,029 --> 00:19:24,629
Oh my god, there's a man covered with blood on the shore!

365
00:19:24,629 --> 00:19:26,529
That guy from the fishman district!

366
00:19:26,929 --> 00:19:28,049
What happened to you?

367
00:19:28,349 --> 00:19:29,469
Someone call a doctor!

368
00:19:29,469 --> 00:19:31,589
Oh, hey!

369
00:19:31,929 --> 00:19:32,689
I'm a doctor!

370
00:19:36,789 --> 00:19:37,189
What?

371
00:19:37,189 --> 00:19:37,629
Hachi?

372
00:19:37,869 --> 00:19:39,049
Who did this?

373
00:19:39,229 --> 00:19:39,929
What happened?

374
00:19:39,929 --> 00:19:43,149
Hachi, it's us!

375
00:19:43,449 --> 00:19:44,329
Chopper and Sanji!

376
00:19:44,729 --> 00:19:45,209
Hold on!

377
00:19:45,589 --> 00:19:46,229
We'll help you!

378
00:19:46,749 --> 00:19:48,289
Why would someone do this?

379
00:19:49,549 --> 00:19:50,689
It's you guys!

380
00:19:51,229 --> 00:19:52,689
I'm happy to see you!

381
00:19:53,129 --> 00:19:54,409
Is Straw Hat here too?

382
00:19:54,969 --> 00:19:56,089
He's not with us!

383
00:19:56,369 --> 00:19:57,289
Don't try to move!

384
00:19:57,529 --> 00:19:58,929
I'll start treating you in a sec!

385
00:19:58,929 --> 00:20:01,609
Wherever your friends are, find them!

386
00:20:01,969 --> 00:20:03,309
And get the hell out of here!

387
00:20:04,849 --> 00:20:07,249
You don't want to get involved, believe me!

388
00:20:07,529 --> 00:20:10,509
Get back on your boat and leave this place while you still can!

389
00:20:10,769 --> 00:20:12,509
Or you'll be fighting for your lives!

390
00:20:13,169 --> 00:20:13,769
Hordeon!

391
00:20:14,289 --> 00:20:14,809
Deccan!

392
00:20:15,389 --> 00:20:15,729
Go!

393
00:20:16,009 --> 00:20:19,209
The new fishman pirates will start attacking the whole island soon!

394
00:20:19,689 --> 00:20:22,669
And once they do, the Ryugu kingdom will fall!

395
00:20:25,669 --> 00:20:26,629
King Neptune!

396
00:20:26,629 --> 00:20:29,469
The princess has been kidnapped!

397
00:20:30,029 --> 00:20:33,089
I don't know how, but they must have broken into the room!

398
00:20:33,489 --> 00:20:35,709
Also, pirates are crashing into the tower!

399
00:20:36,009 --> 00:20:36,749
It's bizarre!

400
00:20:37,049 --> 00:20:39,429
In any case, they'll be here any minute!

401
00:20:40,009 --> 00:20:40,789
Get ready!

402
00:20:41,589 --> 00:20:42,109
Kidnapped?

403
00:20:42,429 --> 00:20:44,249
Somebody's taken away my Shirahoshi?

404
00:20:44,589 --> 00:20:45,389
Who was it?

405
00:20:45,649 --> 00:20:47,329
I'll kill them!

406
00:20:49,329 --> 00:20:51,629
Wait, there's a pirate raid going on?

407
00:20:51,989 --> 00:20:53,249
And they don't mean us?

408
00:20:53,249 --> 00:20:54,689
This is the worst time!

409
00:20:54,689 --> 00:20:57,869
All I want is to get out of here and now it's some kind of pirate party!

410
00:20:58,269 --> 00:20:59,289
We're screwed!

411
00:21:01,009 --> 00:21:01,449
Fine!

412
00:21:01,689 --> 00:21:02,649
Just ignore me!

413
00:21:02,889 --> 00:21:03,349
Jerk!

414
00:21:03,689 --> 00:21:04,329
I'll cut them!

415
00:21:04,449 --> 00:21:06,649
Violence is the last thing we need right now!

416
00:21:06,649 --> 00:21:13,529
If we want to make it out of here alive, we have to open up the gate, no matter what!

417
00:21:13,989 --> 00:21:15,889
Oh no, they're here!

418
00:21:15,889 --> 00:21:24,289
You can come out of the shark now, you know!

419
00:21:24,549 --> 00:21:27,989
Oh, that's okay, I think I'd rather stay inside for now!

420
00:21:29,749 --> 00:21:32,269
Must be nice after being cooped up for ten years!

421
00:21:32,509 --> 00:21:33,969
Yes, my heart is racing!

422
00:21:34,589 --> 00:21:36,489
They're probably worried sick about me!

423
00:21:36,489 --> 00:21:38,469
You've been out five minutes!

424
00:21:38,969 --> 00:21:40,389
Have a little fun, would ya?

425
00:21:41,169 --> 00:21:42,949
Jeez, what a weirdo!

426
00:21:45,309 --> 00:21:47,109
Now I know how it feels!

427
00:21:48,529 --> 00:21:54,669
This is a real adventure, huh?

428
00:21:54,669 --> 00:21:58,449
It sure is!

429
00:21:59,669 --> 00:22:02,669
If your heart's racing, it counts as an adventure!

430
00:22:03,949 --> 00:22:06,249
You mentioned a thing called the Sea Forest, right?

431
00:22:06,569 --> 00:22:07,669
So what is that?

432
00:22:08,029 --> 00:22:09,609
Is it a pretty cool place?

433
00:22:09,609 --> 00:22:14,609
It's a graveyard...

434
00:22:15,149 --> 00:22:20,449
Or rather, there's one grave that I never got to visit because I was locked away.

435
00:22:21,809 --> 00:22:27,189
Ten years I've wanted to go, and now my only dream can finally come true!

436
00:22:27,189 --> 00:22:42,029
It's already been ten long years since her assassination in broad daylight threw Fishman Island into upheaval.

437
00:22:43,189 --> 00:22:44,229
Time flies.

438
00:22:46,109 --> 00:22:50,169
The princes have grown into strong and worthy protectors.

439
00:22:50,989 --> 00:22:54,789
Princess Shirahoshi is locked in the tower, but she is safe.

440
00:22:54,789 --> 00:22:59,989
But as for you, your memory survives.

441
00:23:00,849 --> 00:23:02,569
Your ideals will live on forever.

442
00:23:04,249 --> 00:23:05,489
Queen Otoime.

443
00:23:09,209 --> 00:23:11,629
Horty's plan for revenge is set into motion.

444
00:23:11,869 --> 00:23:18,349
The defenses of the Ryugu Palace have been left wide open thanks to the unexpected actions of the pirates thrown into its walls.

445
00:23:18,349 --> 00:23:27,209
The Straw Hats, who had unwittingly taken control of the palace, must now defend it against the new Fishman Pirates, who pour into its halls, led by Horty himself.

446
00:23:27,409 --> 00:23:35,229
On the next One Piece, Horty's Onslaught, the retaliatory plan set into motion, I'm gonna be King of the Pirates!

